    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d506-a2">

                <pb facs="0910" n="848" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg848"/>

                <opener><dateline rendition="#center">[From the Daily Levant Herald of <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1877-10-02">October 2,
                        1877</date>.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>As a mark of his appreciation of their signal services to the state during the
                    present war, the Sultan has been pleased to confer upon Osman Pasha, for his
                    defense of Plevna, and upon Ahmed Moukhtar Pasha, for his conduct of the
                    campaign in Asia, the title of <hi rendition="#italic">Ghazi</hi> (The
                    Victorious; and the decoration of the imperial order of the Osmanié of the first
                    class, set in diamonds. His Majesty further presents to each of” these gallant
                    generals a jewel-hilted sword and two Arab chargers of the purest breed.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
